SPEC_RELEASE	A release is a signed tag `v<semver>` on `main`; pushing it runs `.github/workflows/release.yml`, which builds the release notes, publishes the GitHub release (`softprops/action-gh-release`) and attests build provenance. Bump `version` in the Justfile and `CITATION.cff` first, in the same PR. This repository is a GitHub *template*: a release changes what every new repository is born with, so re-run `./launcher.sh --doctor` and `bash build/just/provision-check.sh .` on a fresh clone before tagging.
SPEC_CI	`main` is protected by a ruleset with these rule types: `required_signatures`, `required_linear_history`, `non_fast_forward`, `deletion`, `code_scanning`, `code_coverage` and `copilot_code_review` (read 2026-09-30; re-read with `gh api repos/hyperpolymath/rsr-template-repo/rules/branches/main`). Only squash merges are allowed and auto-merge is on. Every commit must be SSH-signed or the PR cannot land. The workflows under `.github/workflows/` are themselves the estate's reference copies: a change here propagates to every repository minted from the template, so change the canonical reusable in `hyperpolymath/standards` first and pin to it here.
SPEC_DECISIONS	Rulings that bind this repository in particular: bun is the only JavaScript runtime (deno, TypeScript, ReScript, Python are banned), A2ML is retired (leave existing `.a2ml` files alone, build nothing new on them), and Justfile changes are mirrored in `.machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile`, which is kept byte-identical.
